Risk and Control – Nodir
Nodir has contributed to strengthening our container security controls through the integration of the VTM library across 3PiiP, UBI and VSaaS. This has helped improve consistency in how vulnerability validation is applied across our Container Security products. He has also completed all mandatory training within the required timelines.
As Nodir continues to develop as a technical lead, I would like him to take a more proactive approach to identifying and managing delivery risks and dependencies. There have been occasions where progress or potential blockers have not been communicated early enough, limiting our opportunity to take action before delivery is affected.
I would also encourage Nodir to make better use of the people and expertise around him to resolve dependencies and move work forward. This includes delegating appropriate activities to the Product Owner or SRE team, contacting relevant stakeholders directly and using clear written updates, rather than relying solely on arranging meetings and waiting for responses.
For example, he can make better use of Avtar's role as PO to manage Jira stories, coordinate communications and engage with users, allowing Nodir to focus more on technical direction and engineering delivery. Similarly, he should work closely with the SRE team and use their expertise to progress requirements such as dashboards, monitoring and alerting, rather than trying to drive every activity himself.
The key expectation is for Nodir to move beyond identifying risks and become more proactive in driving their resolution, while maintaining clear visibility of progress and potential delivery impacts.

Financial Performance – Nodir
Financial Performance – Nodir
Nodir has made a valuable contribution by enhancing the existing Managed Repos page automation, originally developed by Houssem, to automatically synchronise the latest approved base images whenever a new version is published. This is important in helping development teams identify and adopt updated base images more quickly, reducing the manual effort involved in keeping their repositories up to date.
By making approved base image updates more readily available, this work helps teams move away from accumulating technical debt through infrequent, major image upgrades towards a more continuous approach to base image maintenance. This supports more efficient engineering practices, reduces the effort associated with large-scale upgrades and helps teams maintain more secure and up-to-date container images.
Another positive outcome is that the script Nodir developed has also been reused by the SRE team to alert on newly approved base images when they fail VSaaS Gating. This helps us identify issues with newly approved images and ensure that the latest base images remain clean and continue to pass our image scanning and gating controls.
I would like Nodir to build on this work by identifying further opportunities to automate repetitive processes and reduce manual effort across our Container Security products.


